# Playnite addon settings UI

When creating or changing **Add-ons → Extension settings** (or any plugin settings `UserControl`):

- Use **Playnite’s stock WPF controls** only: `CheckBox`, `Label`, `Slider`, `RadioButton`, `ComboBox`, `TextBox`, `Button`, `TextBlock`. Layout with `StackPanel` / `Grid`.
- **Baseline** is **`src/Autogrid/src/AutogridSettingsView.xaml`**: theme `Label` + `CheckBox` + `Slider` / `RadioButton`, `TextBlock` with `{DynamicResource TextBrush}`, Autogrid-like label margins (`0,0,0,4` / `0,16,0,4`). Copy that pattern for new plugins.
- Do **not** invent chrome: custom cards, pills, tab strips, toggles, icon buttons, pickers, shadows, or new typography/colors. No custom `FontSize` / `FontWeight` on `CheckBox` or `Label`.
- If a keyed style is required, **`BasedOn="{StaticResource {x:Type Control}}`** (e.g. `{x:Type CheckBox}` / `{x:Type Label}`). A style without `BasedOn` replaces Playnite’s template (12px WPF chrome).
- Invent a new control **only when the user explicitly asks**. Dependent options still nest under the parent checkbox (see `gamehoverdetails-settings-nesting.mdc`).

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD: custom chrome -->
<Border CornerRadius="8" Background="#1C1C1E">
    <TextBlock FontSize="11" FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Columns" />
</Border>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: Playnite stock, Autogrid baseline -->
<Label Margin="0,16,0,4" Content="Target columns" />
<Slider Minimum="1" Maximum="20" TickFrequency="1" IsSnapToTickEnabled="True"
        Value="{Binding TargetColumns, Mode=TwoWay}" />
```
